{"entryId":"1568","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1568:1","sourceSha256":"fdaa62329604d6366a66e7fd434ae33db6ddc3ed01f5ccdf90d0b3fc80773fa0","englishSha256":"ef178bd5b6f0117f45ace5ce22b37145bb5478b253ca04589c9aef884c3c3e83","citations":[{"id":"1568:1:citation-01","he":[12,37],"en":[14,59],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Shabbat_17b.1.2"},"reference":"Rashi on Shabbat 17b:1:2","assessment":"Rashi on Shabbat glosses the word as a setter of traps for animal and bird. Rashi on Taanit explicitly translates it as bird-catcher and treats Tavot as the name.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rashi on Shabbat 17b:1:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Shabbat_17b.1.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Rashi on Taanit 10a:13:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Taanit_10a.13.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"1568:1:citation-02","he":[38,53],"en":[80,104],"target":{"url":"https://torahwords.org/aru_1512"},"reference":"Arukh, s.v. Rashba, first sense","assessment":"Arukh expressly quotes a Gaon for the house-head interpretation and adduces a Targum expression for household head. It presents the trapping interpretation separately.","evidence":[{"reference":"Arukh, s.v. Rashba, first sense","target":{"url":"https://torahwords.org/aru_1512"},"witness":"Arukh, TorahWords digital transcription"}]},{"id":"1568:1:citation-03","he":[55,79],"en":[151,163],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_146b.8"},"reference":"Shabbat 146b:8","assessment":"Shabbat 146b explicitly has Tavot Rishba transmitting Shmuel’s ruling concerning a myrtle leaf.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 146b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_146b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1568:1:citation-04","he":[81,100],"en":[171,187],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_17b.1"},"reference":"Shabbat 17b:1","assessment":"Shabbat 17b explicitly has Tavi Rishba transmitting a separate ruling of Shmuel; preserve the name forms.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 17b:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_17b.1"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Shabbat 17b:1:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Shabbat_17b.1.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"1568:1:citation-05","he":[102,179],"en":[341,351],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Taanit_10a.13"},"reference":"Taanit 10a:13","assessment":"The checked folio quotes the liturgical words “and give dew and rain” in the question. Rashi gives the seasonal explanation about putting wood into storage.","evidence":[{"reference":"Taanit 10a:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Taanit_10a.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Taanit 10a:13:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Taanit_10a.13.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3,4],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"Rashi explains the title as setting snares for game and birds. Arukh preserves a separate Geonic household interpretation. Keep Tavi and Tavot as surface readings of the two cited passages and retain the exact phrase of the rain request.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Rashi on Shabbat 17b:1:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Shabbat_17b.1.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Rashi on Taanit 10a:13:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Taanit_10a.13.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Shabbat 146b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_146b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shabbat 17b:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_17b.1"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Shabbat 17b:1:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Shabbat_17b.1.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"ref